        "original_id": "c54f316a-3f30-586a-962d-040ba11682f9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Monstera, Cercis, Monstera acuminata\n- Taxonomy: Araceae, Fabaceae, Cercidoideae, genera, species\n- Places: tropical regions of the Americas, warm temperate regions, central Petén, San Luis Potosí\n\nFacts:\n- Monstera is a genus of about 50 species of flowering plants in the arum family Araceae and is native to tropical regions of the Americas.\n- Cercis is a genus of about 10 species in the subfamily Cercidoideae of the pea family Fabaceae and is native to warm temperate regions.\n- Monstera acuminata is abundant in central Petén and extends north to San Luis Potosí.\n- Monstera acuminata is the northernmost species in the genus Monstera.",
